Target theorem verified as fact `ce7644b69bf7fa2b`.

The complete classification is
\[
\boxed{p(x)=x+c \quad\text{or}\quad p(x)=-x+c,\qquad c\in\mathbb R.}
\]

The proof sets \(f=p-x\), expands \(f(x+f(x))\) exactly, and derives \(f\mid 2+f'\). Degree comparison forces every nonconstant \(f\) to satisfy \(f'=-2\); constant \(f\) gives translations. All converse and zero cases were checked.

